      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-182728",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $\\mid R \\cdot R|= c$, complete the following reasoning about the cardinality of the set $R \\cdot [- 1, 5)$:\n\nSince the function $f: (x, y) \u2192 (x, y)$ (that maps any ordered pair to itself) is an injection from $R \\cdot [- 1, 5)$ into $R \\cdot R$, and\n$\\frac{2}{3}$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nis an injection from $R \\cdot R$ onto $R \\cdot (-1, 1)\u2286R \\cdot [- 1, 5)$, according to Cantor-Bernstein-Schr\u00f6der theorem, we have that\n$\\mid R \\cdot [- 1, 5)|=$ {{field-3}}."
