      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-182809",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $\\mid R \\cdot R|= c$, complete the following reasoning about the cardinality of the set $(0, 3] \\cdot R$:\n\nSince the function $f: (x, y) \u2192 (x, y)$ (that maps any ordered pair to itself) is an injection from $(0, 3] \\cdot R$ into $R \\cdot R$, and\n$\\arctan (x)$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nis an injection from $R \\cdot R$ onto $(0, 2) \\cdot R\u2286(0, 3] \\cdot R$, according to Cantor-Bernstein-Schr\u00f6der theorem, we have that\n$\\mid (0, 3] \\cdot R|=$ {{field-3}}."
    },
