      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-183625",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $|R\\times R|=c,$ complete the following reasoning about the cardinality of the set $R\\times [-5,6):$\n\nSince the function $f:(x,y)\\to (x,y)$ (that maps any ordered pair to itself) is an injection from $R\\times [-5,6)$ into $R\\times R,$ and \n\n$$\ng:(x,y)\\to (x,{{field-1}}{{field-2}})\n$$\n\nis an injection from $R\\times R$ onto $R\\times (-5,5)\u2286R\\times [-5,6),$ according to Cantor-Bernstein-Schr\u00f6der theorem, we have that \n$|R\\times [-5,6)|=$ {{field-3}}."
